Give the output component the geometry the filters produce, instead of the
source geometry: the muxer writes the component's size into the container, so a
WebM VP8 track announced 1920x1080 while its frames were 640x360.  H264, HEVC
and VP9 hide it because their bitstreams carry the size; VP8 does not.

Ours, on top of patch 100 (tvheadend#2117); not in uknunknown's branch yet.

--- src/transcoding/transcode/stream.c.orig
+++ src/transcoding/transcode/stream.c
@@ -182,6 +182,19 @@ tvh_stream_setup(TVHStream *self, TVHCodecProfile *profile, tvh_ssc_t *ssc)
         // Deliberately outside the hwaccel guard below -- a software-only
         // build needs this just as much.
         memcpy(&self->context->es_info, ssc, sizeof(elementary_info_t));
+        // The component handed downstream describes the *encoded* stream, so
+        // give it the geometry the filters will produce.  Left at the source
+        // geometry, the muxer writes that into the container: a WebM VP8 track
+        // announcing 1920x1080 while its frames are 640x360.  It goes unnoticed
+        // on H264/HEVC/VP9, whose bitstreams carry the size and let a player
+        // correct the container, but VP8 has no such parser in the way.
+        {
+            const TVHVideoCodecProfile *vp = (TVHVideoCodecProfile *)profile;
+            if (vp->size.num > 0 && vp->size.den > 0) {
+                ssc->es_width  = vp->size.num;
+                ssc->es_height = vp->size.den;
+            }
+        }
 #if ENABLE_MMAL | ENABLE_V4L2M2M | ENABLE_NVENC | ENABLE_VAAPI | ENABLE_QSV
         // record decoder hw accel (to be used later on, for filter selection)
         self->context->iavhwdevtype = avhwdevtype;
